SAR port for AI-CAE4ALL
=======================

The package in sar/ is derived from

    SAR -- "One Scale at a Time: Scale-Autoregressive Modeling for Fluid Flow
    Distributions", Mario Lino and Nils Thuerey (2026), arXiv:2604.11403
    https://github.com/tum-pbs/SAR, commit 1d1609fd

distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE, copied
unchanged from upstream). Hyperparameter defaults follow upstream's
examples/Wing scripts.

Changes made for AI-CAE4ALL (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)). Every modified file
carries an "AI-CAE4ALL port" comment at the change.

Modified
    sar/__init__.py                         drop the datasets/plot/metrics imports
    sar/graph.py                            drop the plot_* helpers (sar/plot.py not vendored)
    sar/loader.py                           torchvision type hint replaced by Optional[Callable]
    sar/nn/__init__.py                      export FlowMatchingModel instead of FlowMatchingTransolver
    sar/nn/flow_matching/__init__.py        drop the fmt.py import
    sar/nn/model.py                         PyTorch Lightning/wandb removed; plain-PyTorch fit loop
                                            with the same optimisation recipe; hparams capture and
                                            load_from_checkpoint reimplemented
    sar/nn/training_settings.py             Lightning/wandb fields removed; loader generator added
    sar/nn/modules/transolver.py            optional memory-lean PhysicsAttention path (same maths)
                                            and optional activation checkpointing
    sar/nn/scale_autoregressive/sar.py      sample_n: count samples, not batches, when splitting
                                            num_samples into sampler batches
    sar/nn/models/__init__.py,
    sar/nn/scale_autoregressive/__init__.py,
    sar/transforms/__init__.py              trailing newline / drop connect.py import

Added
    sar/nn/modules/__init__.py              empty package marker

Not vendored (not needed to train or sample)
    sar/datasets.py, sar/metrics.py, sar/plot.py, sar/nn/callbacks.py,
    sar/nn/flow_matching/fmt.py, sar/transforms/connect.py,
    examples/ (scripts, notebooks, checkpoints), pyproject.toml

Everything outside sar/ (SAR_main.py, general_modules/, training_profiles/,
inference_profiles/, tests/) is AI-CAE4ALL code; general_modules/resume_state.py
is the suite's shared copy.
